<title>UK: UK's Brown briefs cabinet on budget.</title>
<headline>UK's Brown briefs cabinet on budget.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The cabinet needed just 30 minutes at its weekly meeting on Wednesday to rubber-stamp Chancellor of the Exchequer Gordon Brown's budget, the first from a Labour government in 18 years, officials said.</p>
<p>They declined to give any details or estimate how long Brown's speech would last.</p>
<p>&quot;It went down extremely well (at cabinet), just as we're confident it will go down extremely well with the public,&quot; one official said.</p>
